WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.082 --> 00:00:09.279
Long ago, before the gods ruled on Mount Olympus, before humans walked the earth, the Titans brought the world out of chaos.

2
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.700
They were the children of Uranus, the sky, and Gaia, the earth.

3
00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:22.431
They ruled the world with benevolence, and lived among its oceans, fields, and mountains during a golden age.

4
00:00:22.432 --> 00:00:32.655
Cronus, the youngest, battled his father to become ruler of the Titans, and then, with his sister Rhea as his wife, he fathered many children.

5
00:00:32.656 --> 00:00:41.369
His mother had warned him, however, that his own son would one day overthrow him, just as he had defeated Uranus.

6
00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:48.265
So, as each of his children was born, he picked the baby up and swallowed the infant whole.

7
00:00:48.266 --> 00:00:57.736
Only his youngest son, Zeus, was saved, when Rhea tricked her husband by giving him a stone wrapped in a blanket to swallow instead.

8
00:00:57.737 --> 00:01:04.012
Rhea sent Zeus away to the island of Crete, where he could grow up safely in secret.

9
00:01:04.013 --> 00:01:09.228
He was raised on goats' milk and honey and learned to be a fierce warrior.

10
00:01:09.229 --> 00:01:14.180
When Zeus was old enough, he returned to seek vengeance on his father.

11
00:01:14.181 --> 00:01:20.998
After a long and mighty struggle, he defeated Cronus and the many Titans who fought alongside him.

12
00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:29.410
Then he plunged his sword into his father's abdomen, sliced his belly open, and released his brothers and sisters.

13
00:01:29.411 --> 00:01:33.886
Zeus became the king of the gods and ruled the Olympians.

14
00:01:33.887 --> 00:01:43.625
He condemned the defeated Titans to the underworld, but permitted those few who had not fought alongside Cronus to live at the foot of the mountain.

15
00:01:43.626 --> 00:01:51.411
Of these, the brothers Prometheus and Epimetheus were Zeus' favorites, and he allowed them many freedoms.

16
00:01:51.412 --> 00:01:58.550
Epimetheus was grateful and satisfied with his new life, but the clever Prometheus grew bored.

17
00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:08.487
The inventive Titan needed something to entertain him, so one day, he picked up a handful of clay and molded it into the shape of a man.

18
00:02:08.488 --> 00:02:15.177
Prometheus made many men, giving them each two legs, two arms, and five senses.

19
00:02:15.178 --> 00:02:20.781
Then Athena, the goddess of wisdom, breathed life into these shapes.

20
00:02:20.782 --> 00:02:26.645
Soon, the men learned to cook food, build homes, and survive on their own.

21
00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:34.805
Zeus watched with a wary eye as these new beings flourished, but Prometheus was aware of his unease.

22
00:02:34.806 --> 00:02:47.249
To keep his creations safe from Zeus' wrath, he taught the men to worship the king of the gods, and he showed them how to build temples and sacrifice animals to the deities of Mount Olympus.

23
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:54.169
For a long time, the men appeased Zeus with their reverence, but the quiet did not last.

24
00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:59.099
One night, the leader of the men came to Prometheus with a request.

25
00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:07.043
Men were hungry for the taste of meat, and Prometheus' visitor begged him to let them eat the sacrificial animals.

26
00:03:07.044 --> 00:03:13.006
Prometheus, who loved these beings very much, did not want to see them unhappy.

27
00:03:13.007 --> 00:03:17.309
So he told them to give him the animal for their next sacrifice.

28
00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:34.340
He took the meat and divided it into two piles: the first pile contained all the good meat, but covered by the animal's unappetizing stomach and innards; the second pile was only bones, hidden under a delectable layer of juicy fat.

29
00:03:34.341 --> 00:03:42.700
When Zeus came to judge which portion should be for the gods and which for the men, he chose, of course, the second pile.

30
00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:50.263
When he returned with it to Mount Olympus and discovered that he had been fooled, he burst into a rage.

31
00:03:50.264 --> 00:03:56.730
From his mountain peak, he sent thunderbolts and a fierce rain down onto the earth below.

32
00:03:56.731 --> 00:04:03.573
Prometheus visited the men after the storm and was distraught to see them huddled together in misery.

33
00:04:03.574 --> 00:04:06.279
The men were cold and hungry.

34
00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:15.671
Prometheus asked Epimetheus to watch over his suffering creations and then, quickly and quietly, climbed to the top of Mount Olympus.

35
00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:23.044
At the summit, he snatched a bundle of burning branches from Zeus' hearth and hurried back down the mountain.

36
00:04:23.045 --> 00:04:26.412
He passed the god's fire to the men.

37
00:04:26.413 --> 00:04:33.925
When Prometheus returned to his home at the base of Mount Olympus, he found the king of the gods blocking the way.

38
00:04:33.926 --> 00:04:39.377
Zeus grabbed Prometheus by the neck and lifted him high off the ground.

39
00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:48.726
Then he hurled the Titan into the underworld, calling on Hades, the god of the underworld, to punish Prometheus with an eternity of pain.

40
00:04:48.727 --> 00:05:00.751
Prometheus was chained to a tall rock, and every morning, a great eagle tore his liver from his body, only for it to grow back each night and be plucked out again the next day.

41
00:05:00.752 --> 00:05:08.353
Epimetheus was devastated by his brother's punishment, but thankful to have escaped Zeus' retribution himself.

42
00:05:08.354 --> 00:05:14.058
Zeus, however, was plotting a very different sort of punishment for Epimetheus.

43
00:05:14.059 --> 00:05:22.622
First, Zeus paid a visit to the god of fire and forge, Hephaestus, and demanded that he create a mortal woman.

44
00:05:22.623 --> 00:05:27.995
Then, he asked his fellow gods and goddesses to adorn her with gifts.

45
00:05:27.996 --> 00:05:42.605
Aphrodite, the goddess of love, gave her the beauty to attract any man to her side; Athena gave her the skills she would need on earth; and Hermes, the messenger of the gods, gave her the power of speech.

46
00:05:42.606 --> 00:05:48.487
They named her Pandora. Her final gift came from Zeus: a sealed jar.

47
00:05:48.488 --> 00:06:00.320
Prometheus had long warned his brother not to accept gifts from the gods, but when Zeus presented Pandora to him, Epimetheus was captivated by her beauty and eloquence.

48
00:06:00.321 --> 00:06:07.352
They were married within days, and the humans rejoiced at the favor Zeus had shown to their protector.

49
00:06:07.353 --> 00:06:18.503
Epimetheus asked Pandora about the jar, and she explained that Zeus had given her explicit instructions that the jar was to be admired but never opened.

50
00:06:18.504 --> 00:06:25.630
Epimetheus took the jar and placed it high on a shelf in his home, where he could look upon it fondly.

51
00:06:25.631 --> 00:06:29.973
Pandora was beautiful and intelligent and loved to learn.

52
00:06:29.974 --> 00:06:35.204
She explored nearby mountains and discovered new herbs to grow in the garden.

53
00:06:35.205 --> 00:06:42.014
She read the tablets carved in the temples and understood the importance of sacrificing to the gods.

54
00:06:42.015 --> 00:06:44.172
She was always curious.

55
00:06:44.173 --> 00:06:50.125
So when she looked at the jar sitting on the shelf, she wondered what secrets it held.

56
00:06:50.126 --> 00:06:56.744
"What could be inside?" she asked herself. "Why did Zeus tell us never to open it?"

57
00:06:56.745 --> 00:07:01.800
Pandora reached up and lifted the jar from its perch on the shelf.

58
00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:08.149
Holding it carefully in her hands, she carried it to a chair by the fireplace and sat down.

59
00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:15.761
Pandora knew she should not defy the wishes of Zeus and her husband, but her curiosity overwhelmed her.

60
00:07:15.762 --> 00:07:21.602
Slowly, she loosened the lid and lifted it just enough to peek inside.

61
00:07:21.603 --> 00:07:32.697
A great force rushed from the jar! In a thick, black cloud, all the evils of the world poured out: hatred, jealousy, fear, greed, and anger.

62
00:07:32.698 --> 00:07:40.586
Pandora quickly realized her mistake and slammed the lid back on the jar, trapping one last item inside.

63
00:07:40.587 --> 00:07:44.014
Watching from Mount Olympus, Zeus smiled.

64
00:07:44.015 --> 00:07:51.808
His punishment was complete; humankind would be beset with strife and plagued by sorrow for all eternity.

65
00:07:51.809 --> 00:07:57.241
Pandora carefully replaced the jar on the shelf with its one treasure still inside.

66
00:07:57.242 --> 00:08:00.509
Inside the jar remained hope.

